  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "tt_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -334
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Typing Toy\n\nType! Each letter you type drops in with a bounce, a spin and a puff of sparks, then keeps bobbing on a slow wave; the colours run across the line like a rainbow seen through the letters. Backspace deletes, Enter starts a new line, Clear (or 48 letters) starts over. Press Focus on the preview first, so the editor's own shortcuts (Delete, Tab, F …) stay out of the way.\n\nHow it works: Keyboard in `text` mode keeps the typed string. Glyphs splits it into one layer per letter with its position, and a Write* → Read* pair (\"letter births\") remembers the time each letter appeared. A ForEach turns each letter's age (now − its birth time) into an elastic scale, a fall (a decay Envelope) and a wobble (a boing Envelope); Mask shows a moving gradient through the letters.",
        "width": 470,
        "height": 270
      }
    },
